{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Remember for Abraham, for Isaac, and for Israel Your servants</b> — here he put the fathers before \"Your servants,\" and in the parashah of Ekev, \"Remember for Your servants, for Abraham\" etc. — he put \"Your servants\" before the fathers, to say that they were His servants from beginning to end. Like its parallel: \"David My servant\" and \"My servant David.\""], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:55.791744106Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}